{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
  "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government claims in this case that Congress decided to treat retaliation against Federal workers who complain of age discrimination differently than every other species of retaliatory conduct, that for age-based retaliation alone Congress created a four-part patchwork scheme in which a small cadre of Federal employees have a full judicial remedy, but tens of thousands of others who suffer retaliatory conduct have absolutely no remedies at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Excuse me. By its plain terms?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Read it to me, would you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of you, as this Court explained in Jackson itself, it's improper to narrow the scope of a stand-alone general discrimination ban that does not identify any discriminatory practices based on a comparison with an enumeration ban that sets forth a detailed series of prohibitions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, why would Congress have taken this drafting approach?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "could have added Federal employers to the definition of employer and subjected them to the private sector regime there, but instead it created a stand-alone prohibition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What about review under -- by the Merit Systems Protection Board?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Age Discrimination and Employment Act does not expressly prohibit retaliation in the Federal sector context and it should not be read to impliedly prohibits such conduct either."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Would it be -- would it be unkind to say that the government's position seems to be that a general ban on discrimination includes a ban on retaliation except when the government is being sued?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can you say what the government's position is on Title VII, whether there is a retaliation remedy against the Federal Government?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, is it any more anomalous than the fact that the only protection of the age protection is simply for people over 40?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: What the courts have focused on is the \"any employee\" language of section 623d of the private sector provisions. And that's the way --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Garre, can I go back to the authority you're pointing out for a moment? Is it your reading of 631a, the private sector section, that says \"the prohibitions in this chapter shall be limited to individuals who are at least 40 years of age,\" that it's correctly read as the prohibitions in this chapter, except those contained in 623a, shall be limited? That's the way you read it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: Well, we -- no, Justice Stevens. I think that the textual argument that the courts have embraced with respect to 623d, the anti-retaliation provision, is because in 623d the Congress specifically said \"with respect to any employees or applicants.\" It couldn't have meant with respect to only 40, only employees who are over 40."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Am I right now in thinking, just as a matter of practice, where there is retaliation, a claim of retaliation in respect to race discrimination, Federal Government, that the person making that claim can go to the EEOC and then to court? That's right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guerra",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GUERRA: I'd like to make three points. First, I want to emphasize the practical reality that there are thousands of employees who have no remedies under any of the schemes we are talking about: Employees of TVA, employees of the General Accounting Office, these employees of the Transportation Security Administration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guerra",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our argument is that it makes no sense to give some people remedies under one scheme and leave some -- congressional employees getting full remedial relief, people under the CSRA getting a limited remedial relief, others getting remedies under the collective bargaining rights and thousands of others have no remedies only with respect --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guerra",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because they simply have none of the remedies the Government has put before --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that because they may not engage in collective bargaining, or because they have chosen not to?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Who -- who is such a person?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why can't they -- why can't they go to like the Merit System Protection Board?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guerra",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They are excluded from the Civil Service Reform Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guerra",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They don't have bargaining rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guerra",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, they have claims for discrimination if they suffer age discrimination directly, but if they complain about age discrimination and then get fired in retaliation, they have nothing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So they are outside the Civil Service, and they don't have unions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They don't have a union?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guerra",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would also like to note that there was a suggestion that perhaps Congress didn't care as much about age discrimination. That's refuted by the House report that accompanied this very statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You should have given us the statute to look at if that's the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guerra",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ee85ab0f9b2d14fbe7ea29415c1d1f412050c81be1e65e782a08a3ec8282e6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ee85ab0f9b2-0003-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "By incorporating that same language in the ADEA's federal sector provision, Congress necessarily gave it the same scope; and, by doing so, eliminated the various anomalies, to put it mildly, that the Government's position leads to."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1321",
      "confidence": 0.0,
